<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stepan Klochurak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1895">1895</a>–<a href="/years/1980">1980</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stepan Klochurak was a Ukrainian politician from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-ruthenia">Carpathian Ruthenia</a> who led the local government of the Hutsul Republic at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yasinia">Yasinia</a> in 1919, which sought union with the Ukrainian People's Republic. In 1938–1939 he was a minister of Carpatho-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, and he later spent years in Soviet labour camps.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stepan-klochurak.jpg" alt="Stepan Klochurak" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stepan_Klochurak_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
